     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"></p>Just thinking out loud...<br><br>The first thing I have discovered is that geom_bar() is not the appropriate geom to use in this instance. I need to use geom_rect().<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">DATA </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">frame</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Xmin</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0L</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0L</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0L</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                   </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Xmax</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> factor</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;High&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Medium&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Low&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> levels </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Low&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Medium&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;High&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                   </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Ymin</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                   </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Ymax</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                   </span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>ggplot</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">DATA</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> aes</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">xmin </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Xmin</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> xmax </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Xmax</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ymin </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Ymin</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ymax </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Ymax</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> fill </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Xmax</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  geom_rect</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  scale_x_discrete</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">labels </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Low&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Medium&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;High&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  scale_y_continuous</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">limits </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">4</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> breaks </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">4</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> labels </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;First&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Second&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Third&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Fourth&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  scale_fill_manual</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">name </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Risk level&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> values </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;darkgreen&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;orange&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;red&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  coord_polar</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">theta </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;y&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>This produces:<br><p style=\"clear:both;text-align:left\"><a style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-ZaPr38Swnho/VK3W3LPd4oI/AAAAAAAACLw/d9NxXGAv8Zs/s1600/Rplot.png\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-ZaPr38Swnho/VK3W3LPd4oI/AAAAAAAACLw/d9NxXGAv8Zs/s1600/Rplot.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792369793015000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2lw4nwC2oNBlNPeMXCLI5F\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-ZaPr38Swnho/VK3W3LPd4oI/AAAAAAAACLw/d9NxXGAv8Zs/s1600/Rplot.png\" border=\"0\"></a></p><p style=\"clear:both;text-align:left\">The obvious thing that I have noticed is that the areas of the segments appear roughly the same - despite the fact that the angles are 0.1, 0.2, and 0.7, respectively. I might have to resort to using a geom_line() where the length of the line represents the proportion of risk and the colour scale will represent the risk level.</p><p style=\"clear:both;text-align:left\"><br></p><p style=\"clear:both;text-align:left\"><br></p><p style=\"clear:both;text-align:left\"><br></p><p style=\"clear:both;text-align:left\"><br><a style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-ZaPr38Swnho/VK3W3LPd4oI/AAAAAAAACLw/d9NxXGAv8Zs/s1600/Rplot.png\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-ZaPr38Swnho/VK3W3LPd4oI/AAAAAAAACLw/d9NxXGAv8Zs/s1600/Rplot.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792369793015000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2lw4nwC2oNBlNPeMXCLI5F\"></a></p></div>"
